# Module 1 – Introduction to RTL Design and ASIC Flow

## 1. QFN-48

QFN stands for **Quad Flat No-lead**.

QFN-48 is a semiconductor package with 48 external electrical connections. It is used to connect the silicon die inside the package to the external PCB.

### Key Points

- QFN = Quad Flat No-lead
- 48 = Number of external connections
- The package does not have long leads extending from the sides.
- It provides good electrical and thermal performance.
- The silicon die is placed inside the package.

---

## 2. Pads

A **pad** is a physical connection point on a chip.

Pads provide the interface between the internal circuitry and the external package connections.

### Functions of Pads

- Connect the chip to the package.
- Provide input and output connections.
- Supply power and ground.
- Allow signals to enter and leave the chip.

### Basic Structure

    External Pin
         |
         v
        PAD
         |
         v
    Internal Circuit

---

## 3. Core

The **core** is the main area of the chip where the internal digital circuitry is placed.

It contains the logic required to implement the design.

### The Core Can Contain

- Standard cells
- Flip-flops
- Combinational logic
- Clock circuitry
- Memories
- Other functional blocks

The core is surrounded by the input/output interface and other physical structures.

---

## 4. Die

The **die** is the actual piece of semiconductor material containing the integrated circuit.

It is usually made from silicon.

The die can contain:

- Core
- I/O cells
- Pads
- Standard cells
- Macros
- Interconnections

### Basic Relationship

    Package
       |
       v
      Die
       |
       +---- Core
       |
       +---- I/O
       |
       +---- Pads
       |
       +---- Macros

---

## 5. Macros

A **macro** is a relatively large pre-designed block used inside an integrated circuit.

Macros are generally more complex than standard cells.

### Examples

- SRAM
- ROM
- PLL
- ADC
- DAC
- Large IP blocks

Macros are generally treated as physical blocks during floorplanning.

