## 28. Specification

The first stage is defining what the chip should do.

The specification describes:

- Required functionality
- Inputs
- Outputs
- Performance requirements
- Power requirements
- Area requirements
- Operating conditions

---

## 29. Architecture

The architecture defines how the required functionality will be implemented.

It determines:

- Major blocks
- Data paths
- Control logic
- Memory requirements
- Communication interfaces
- Clocking structure

### Example

    CPU
     |
     +---- Memory
     |
     +---- UART
     |
     +---- GPIO
     |
     +---- SPI

---

## 30. RTL Design

RTL stands for **Register Transfer Level**.

RTL describes the behavior and structure of a digital circuit using HDLs such as:

- Verilog
- SystemVerilog
- VHDL

RTL describes:

- Registers
- Combinational logic
- Sequential logic
- Data transfers
- Control logic

### Example

    always @(posedge clk)
        q <= d;

This describes a flip-flop.

---

